```

## 4. Validation escalation handlers

**Escalation wiring** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`):
- `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` → `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.ValidationExceptionHandler`
- `java.lang.Exception.yml` → `GeneralExceptionHandler`
- Also present: `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml`, `...NotFoundException.yml`, `...AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/ValidationExceptionHandler.java`**
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.Objects;

import net.officefloor.plugin.section.clazz.Parameter;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ProblemDetail;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.ValidationMessageDto;
import org.springframework.validation.BindingResult;
import org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException;

public class ValidationExceptionHandler {

    public void handle(@Parameter MethodArgumentNotValidException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response) {
        ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
                "The request contains invalid or missing parameters");
        BindingResult bindingResult = ex.getBindingResult();
        if (bindingResult.hasErrors()) {
            List<ValidationMessageDto> schemaValidationErrors = bindingResult.getFieldErrors().stream()
                    .map(fieldError -> {
                        String rejectedValue = Objects.toString(fieldError.getRejectedValue(), "null");
                        String defaultMessage = Objects.toString(fieldError.getDefaultMessage(), "Validation failed");
                        String message = "Field '%s' %s (rejected value: %s)".formatted(
                                fieldError.getField(), defaultMessage, rejectedValue);
                        return new ValidationMessageDto(message)
                                .putAdditionalProperty("field", fieldError.getField())
                                .putAdditionalProperty("rejectedValue", rejectedValue)
                                .putAdditionalProperty("defaultMessage", defaultMessage);
                    })
                    .toList();
            detail.setProperty("schemaValidationErrors", schemaValidationErrors);
        }
        response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(detail));
    }
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/ProblemDetails.java`** (shared builder):
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

import java.net.URI;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.List;

import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ProblemDetail;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.ValidationMessageDto;

final class ProblemDetails {

    private ProblemDetails() {
    }

    static ProblemDetail build(Exception ex, HttpStatus status, String detail) {
        ProblemDetail problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatus(status);
        problemDetail.setType(URI.create("about:blank"));
        problemDetail.setTitle(ex.getClass().getSimpleName());
        problemDetail.setDetail(detail);
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now());
        problemDetail.setProperty("schemaValidationErrors", List.<ValidationMessageDto>of());
        return problemDetail;
    }
}
```

**`GeneralExceptionHandler.java`** produces a 500 for any other `Exception`.

**How a 400 is currently produced:** `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` in `BuildOwner` throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → `ValidationExceptionHandler` builds an RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` (status 400, `title` = exception simple name, `detail`, `timestamp`) and attaches a **`schemaValidationErrors`** array — each element a `ValidationMessageDto` with a `message` plus additional properties `field`, `rejectedValue`, `defaultMessage`. `ValidationMessageDto` is generated from the `ValidationMessage` schema (`openapi.yml` lines 1954-1967, `additionalProperties: true`).

Important mismatch to note: the current handler emits the error list under the property name **`schemaValidationErrors`**, but the acceptance test (below) asserts a top-level **`$.errors`** array of bare field-name strings. The existing code does not currently produce an `errors` array.

## 5. Tests for creating owners (400/validation)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** (full):
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.jsonPath;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.status;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** required-fields: Reject creating an owner that is missing or blank in any of firstName, lastName, address,... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void errorRejectsMissingCity() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
		o.remove("city");
		createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest())
				.andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors").value(org.hamcrest.Matchers.hasItem("city")));
	}

	@Test
	void errorRejectsBlankTelephone() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
		o.put("telephone", "   ");
		createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAcceptsCompleteOwner() throws Exception {
		createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```
This test asserts a 400 with `$.errors` containing the string `"city"` for a missing field, a 400 for a blank telephone, and 2xx for a complete owner.

**Base class `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the harness (full contents were read). Key relevant pieces:
- Annotated `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username = "acceptance-admin", roles = {"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`.
- `ownerNode()` builds a valid payload with `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`.
- `createOwner(JsonNode body)` does `POST /api/owners` with JSON content; `getOwner(id)` does `GET /api/owners/{id}`; `extractId(...)` reads `id` from body or the `Location` header.
- Uses `tools.jackson` (Jackson 3) `ObjectMapper`/`ObjectNode`.

Other test files present: `AuditLogCapture.java` in the same package. No other owner-specific test classes exist.

## 6. Build system and test command

Build tool: **Maven**, build file **`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`** (Maven wrapper `mvnw`/`mvnw.cmd` present; no Gradle).

Relevant build detail: DTOs are generated during `generate-sources` by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (generatorName `spring`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`, `modelPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, `performBeanValidation=true`, `useJakartaEe=true`); generated sources are added from `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`. Tests are JUnit 5 (Jupiter) run by the standard Surefire lifecycle (no custom Surefire config).

Test commands:
- All tests: `./mvnw test`
- Full verify: `./mvnw verify`
- Just the acceptance test class: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`

(Because DTOs are generated, tests require the full `generate-sources`/compile phases — i.e. run via `./mvnw test`, not a bare compile of the hand-written sources.)

